     "text": [
      "Are customers more likely to leave a positive review (4+) or negative review (< 3) based on their product experience?\n",
      "    \n",
      "Yes, they are.\n",
      "    \n",
      "Based on the data, customers are much more likely to leave a review when they had a positive experience\n",
      "(4★ or higher) compared to when they had a negative one (less than 3★). Across all manufacturers, \n",
      "the number of positive reviews is far higher than the number of negative reviews. In many cases, \n",
      "positive reviews make up almost all the reviews a product receives. This shows that most people \n",
      "who choose to leave feedback do so because they are satisfied with their purchase, not because \n",
      "they are unhappy.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ARE CUSTOMER MORE LIKELY TO LEAVE A REVIEW IF THE PRODUCT WAS A POSITIVE EXPERIENCE(4★+)  VERSUS A NEGATIVE EXPERIENCE(<3★)?\n",
    "\n",
    "import plotly.express as px\n",
    "\n",
    "# Combine positive & negative into one dataframe\n",
    "review_data = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"manufacturer\": manufacturers,\n",
    "    \"Positive Reviews (4★+)\": positive_review_counts,\n",
    "    \"Negative Reviews (<3★)\": negative_review_counts\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "# Melt into long format\n",
    "review_melted = review_data.melt(\n",
    "    id_vars=\"manufacturer\",\n",
    "    value_vars=[\"Positive Reviews (4★+)\", \"Negative Reviews (<3★)\"],\n",
    "    var_name=\"Review Type\",\n",
    "    value_name=\"Count\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = px.bar(\n",
    "    review_melted,\n",
    "    x=\"manufacturer\",\n",
    "    y=\"Count\",\n",
    "    color=\"Review Type\",\n",
    "    title=\"Share of Positive vs Negative Reviews per Manufacturer (100% Stacked)\",\n",
    "    barmode=\"relative\",     # key part for 100% ratio bars\n",
    "    text_auto=True\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.update_layout(\n",
    "    yaxis_title=\"Proportion of Reviews\",\n",
    "    hovermode=\"x unified\",\n",
    "    height=600\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\"\"Are customers more likely to leave a positive review (4+) or negative review (< 3) based on their product experience?\n",
    "    \n",
    "Yes, they are.\n",
    "    \n",
    "Based on the data, customers are much more likely to leave a review when they had a positive experience\n",
    "(4★ or higher) compared to when they had a negative one (less than 3★). Across all manufacturers, \n",
    "the number of positive reviews is far higher than the number of negative reviews. In many cases, \n",
    "positive reviews make up almost all the reviews a product receives. This shows that most people \n",
    "who choose to leave feedback do so because they are satisfied with their purchase, not because \n",
    "they are unhappy.\"\"\")\n"
   ]
